!path "/reconnect"

---
from pywire import wire

connection_status = wire("connected")
ping_count = wire(0)

@after_update
def track_update(self):
    ping_count.value += 1
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Reconnect Overlay — v0.4</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 720px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
    h1 { color: #6366f1; }
    button { padding: .5rem 1.2rem; background: #ef4444; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; margin: .3rem; }
    button.safe { background: #6366f1; }
    .result { background: #f0fdf4; border: 1px solid #86efac; border-radius: 4px; padding: .5rem; margin-top: .5rem; font-family: monospace; }
    .back { color: #6366f1; text-decoration: none; font-size: .9rem; }
    .instructions { background: #fef3c7; border: 1px solid #fbbf24; border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
    code { background: #f3f4f6; padding: .1rem .3rem; border-radius: 3px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="back" href="/">← Back</a>
  <h1>Reconnect Overlay</h1>

  <div class="instructions">
    <strong>How to test:</strong>
    <ol>
      <li>Click "Disconnect WebSocket" — the custom reconnect overlay (<code>#v04-reconnect-panel</code>) should appear</li>
      <li>Wait ~2–5 seconds — the client will automatically attempt to reconnect</li>
      <li>Once reconnected, the overlay disappears and the update count resumes</li>
      <li>Or: use DevTools → Network → throttle to "Offline" and back</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div>
    <button id="disconnect-btn" onclick="window.pywire && window.pywire.disconnect(); console.log('[reconnect-test] disconnect called')">
      Disconnect WebSocket
    </button>
    <button class="safe" id="ping-btn" @click={track_update}>Send Update (update count: {ping_count})</button>
  </div>

  <div class="result" id="conn-status">Status: {connection_status}</div>

  <div style="margin-top:2rem;padding:1rem;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:6px;">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0">WS Keep-Alive Verification</h3>
    <p>With <code>ws_ping_interval=5</code>, ping frames are sent every 5 seconds.</p>
    <p>Check: DevTools → Network → WS connection → Frames tab → look for binary ping/pong frames</p>
    <p>Or open the Console and look for PyWire debug messages.</p>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
